{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/857445-i-am-worried-solars-won-t-be-the-best-at-shapeshifting-in-3e","id":857445,"title":"I am worried Solars won't be the best at shapeshifting in 3e.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-01T20:45:22-07:00","id":857445,"title":"I am worried Solars won't be the best at shapeshifting in 3e.","content":"The 3e core is really cool, but reading it, there's one thing about it that kind of bothers me.<br /> <br /> It feels like Solars aren't going to be the best at shapeshifting in 3e.<br /> <br /> Now, I know what you're thinking. &quot;Aquillion, don't be silly! The Solars are obviously the best at shapeshifting!&quot; But bear with me. First, there's the Solar theme section, which doesn't really go into enough detail on how Solars shapeshift or what shapeshifting themes they explore. Granted, I know space is limited, but you'd think a few pages devoted to that would have been worth it so we could use it to guide our homebrow Solar shapeshifting charms!<br /> <br /> Additionally, the game describes Lunars as &quot;peerless shapeshifters&quot;, which certainly raises some eyebrows. Granted this is technically correct (Solars are not their <i>peers</i>, they are better!), but it seems odd to talk so much about it.<br /> <br /> Also, there is the total lack of any sort of Solar shapeshifting charms anywhere at all in the Solar charmset. Again, I know space was tight, but a few dozen Solar shapeshifting charms could have fit in somewhere, surely? The caste descriptions also lack any real in-depth discussion of how they each approach shapeshifting in their individual ways.<br /> <br /> Now, I know I'm just worrying over nothing, so please reassure me! Explain what awesome shapeshifters Solars will be in 3e. I assume that there will be many more Solar shapeshifting charms in, for instance, the Lunars book, since apparently that book is going to touch on shapeshifting a bit? I don't know, it seems like an odd place to put those charms, but I know how wordcount can be.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">(With 15 minutes to spare! In EST, anyway.)</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 04-01-2016, 11:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T20:47:38-07:00","id":857447,"title":"","content":"Well there's nothing <i>canon</i>, but I think upgrade charms building on Perfect Mirror would be good homebrew territory for this. If you can already replicate someone else's anima banner and float a few inches above the ground it stands to reason that you can replicate something like a bird's wings too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T21:14:22-07:00","id":857467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/857445-i-am-worried-solars-won-t-be-the-best-at-shapeshifting-in-3e#post857445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, I know I'm just worrying over nothing, so please reassure me! Explain what awesome shapeshifters Solars will be in 3e. I assume that there will be many more Solar shapeshifting charms in, for instance, the Lunars book, since apparently that book is going to touch on shapeshifting a bit? I don't know, it seems like an odd place to put those charms, but I know how wordcount can be.[/SIZE]</div> </div> </div> </div>Solar shapeshifting is going to be in Arms of the Chosen - it's literal, like, the many different arms they can sprout and use. I recall a dev quote where each arm could be attuned to a specific Ability, granting the Solar the power to temporarily access any Ess 1 or 2 Charm in that Ability's Charm tree. This fits pretty well with a lot of the Hindu-Buddhist mythology Exalted draws on, where great religious leaders are depicted with many, many arms. And we all know being religious leaders is something Solars are the best at.<br /> <br /> IIRC Arms of the Chosen is going to be about 64 pages, so that means 100+ Charms of Solar shapeshifting. Don't panic yet dude, it's going to be awesome.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">two and a half hours left in pst</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/K9a6Pmp.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/998-korhal_iv","name":"Korhal_IV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"592"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T21:23:06-07:00","id":857469,"title":"","content":"Solar shapeshifting is an outgrowth of human shapeshifting, which means the changes humans are capable of performing in and on themselves. They have an unmatched ability to transform horrible realities into shining futures, ignorance into wisdom, sorrow into grace, and weakness into strength. Their special capability, which other Exalts can only barely replicate and usually have no charms for, is to do the same for others. Look at Harmonious Academic Methodology, can you imagine a Lunar even trying to transform others so radically? A Lunar can turn into a snake. (It never helps.) A solar can transform a desert backwater into the Serpent Empire that conquers half a direction. Now who is really the better shapeshifter now? I don't see Lunars getting ten thousand arms tens of miles long to fight armies in different countries.<br /> <br /> The reason it doesn't get a lot of mention is because it is so interwoven into everything they do. With one bureaucracy charm and a few rolls they can transform themselves into merchant princes. With one charm they transform themselves into sorcerers. Survival is overflowing with ways to shapeshift animals into god-beasts. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">I like it best when people aren't sure if its a joke or not.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T21:29:55-07:00","id":857475,"title":"","content":"Sorcerous Workings.<br /> <br /> I swear, some people haven't even read the book.<br /> <br /> Sorcerous Workings are Solar's flexible, powerful, and wide-ranging tool that allows them to shapeshift and bend fate as well as (if not even better) in previous editions.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T21:44:31-07:00","id":857486,"title":"","content":"On top of Sorcerous Workings, Martial Arts (gazellecarp!) and Sorcerous Workings, there's also Lore charms.<br /> <br /> Now, I've read the book, but if there's anything I've learned it's that the internet is always right, and by that metric, Lore charms allow Solars to become unstoppable destroyers of civilizations.<br /> <br /> And really, with that kind of reality-warping power, all a Lore Supernal Solar needs to do is simply declare themselves to be a tyrant lizard, and it is so.<br /> <br /> The ST naturally gets no say in this whatsoever, despite this edition professing it's complete trust in said Storyteller.<br /> <br /> Oh, and then a Solar craftsmen can just build Doombots of himself that happen to be in the shape of claw striders. Because he has so much XP lying around. Obviously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T21:48:34-07:00","id":857491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/857445-i-am-worried-solars-won-t-be-the-best-at-shapeshifting-in-3e?p=857486#post857486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On top of Sorcerous Workings, Martial Arts (gazellecarp!) and Sorcerous Workings, there's also Lore charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Common misconception: you actually don't need charms to introduce a fact. 3 dots is enough, and with that and a Solar excellency you can easily hit the required difficulty to introduce the fact that you're a shapeshifter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T21:50:22-07:00","id":857493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/857445-i-am-worried-solars-won-t-be-the-best-at-shapeshifting-in-3e#post857445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 3e core is really cool, but reading it, there's one thing about it that kind of bothers me.<br /> <br /> It feels like Solars aren't going to be the best at shapeshifting in 3e.<br /> <br /> Now, I know what you're thinking. &quot;Aquillion, don't be silly! The Solars are obviously the best at shapeshifting!&quot; But bear with me. First, there's the Solar theme section, which doesn't really go into enough detail on how Solars shapeshift or what shapeshifting themes they explore. Granted, I know space is limited, but you'd think a few pages devoted to that would have been worth it so we could use it to guide our homebrow Solar shapeshifting charms!<br /> <br /> Additionally, the game describes Lunars as &quot;peerless shapeshifters&quot;, which certainly raises some eyebrows. Granted this is technically correct (Solars are not their <i>peers</i>, they are better!), but it seems odd to talk so much about it.<br /> <br /> Also, there is the total lack of any sort of Solar shapeshifting charms anywhere at all in the Solar charmset. Again, I know space was tight, but a few dozen Solar shapeshifting charms could have fit in somewhere, surely? The caste descriptions also lack any real in-depth discussion of how they each approach shapeshifting in their individual ways.<br /> <br /> Now, I know I'm just worrying over nothing, so please reassure me! Explain what awesome shapeshifters Solars will be in 3e. I assume that there will be many more Solar shapeshifting charms in, for instance, the Lunars book, since apparently that book is going to touch on shapeshifting a bit? I don't know, it seems like an odd place to put those charms, but I know how wordcount can be.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">(With 15 minutes to spare! In EST, anyway.)</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh HAH HAH Very clever! You don't think that we know that you know that we know you might not know that you're actually a Lunar in disguise?! Because trust me, WE KNOW! It's all part of your clever ruse to make us allllllllllllllll think that the Lunars invented shapeshifting when it was really the Solars all along. You just want to tell more of those sob stories like how Lunars invented Solar Circle Sorcery and Twilight Meanie Mcmeanieface(No relation to Boatie, that is obviously an Eclipse. Sail and whatnot hello!) came along and took it. I can see your Tell buddy and we all know THOSE will be back for 3e!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T21:53:26-07:00","id":857495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/857445-i-am-worried-solars-won-t-be-the-best-at-shapeshifting-in-3e?p=857491#post857491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Common misconception: you actually don't need charms to introduce a fact. 3 dots is enough, and with that and a Solar excellency you can easily hit the required difficulty to introduce the fact that you're a shapeshifter.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's objectively suboptimal though. You don't ever need to introduce the fact that you're a shapeshifter, afterall who would deny the Unconquered Sun's good-old T-Rex days? Surely not any mortal that cares about their meager existence. And as a solar, you get a piece of that action.<br /> <br /> Nah, Solar shapeshifting is such that you simply introduce the fact that you are a mouse, or flying away, or have already turned into the target's kids.<br /> <br /> Another example includes:<br /> [rolls Lore] I'm on a horse.<br /> [rolls Lore] The horse is now diamonds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T22:16:36-07:00","id":857503,"title":"","content":"Personally I'm more worried about their lack of elemental abilities. There's a solid base for Shapeshifting to build off of with Perfect Mirror, and the Fact Introducing charms serve as a foundation for later Fate manipulation charms, but there's absolutely nothing that will allow them to start mastering the elements in the corebook. It's possible they may be able to do so with the Immaculate styles, but there really should be a native option to allow them total mastery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2034,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","user":"JayTee","date":". 04-02-2016, 01:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T22:23:47-07:00","id":857505,"title":"","content":"JayTee, I'm afraid you're wrong, there's literally a merit for shooting fire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/857445-i-am-worried-solars-won-t-be-the-best-at-shapeshifting-in-3e?p=857475#post857475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorcerous Workings.<br /> <br /> I swear, some people haven't even read the book.<br /> <br /> Sorcerous Workings are Solar's flexible, powerful, and wide-ranging tool that allows them to shapeshift and bend fate as well as (if not even better) in previous editions.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly! Giving yourself a magical power is a Celestial 2 working. For a Solar sorcerer, that's 2xp to give yourself the power to turn into a T-Rex (and it doesn't require you to hunt down a T-Rex prior to the ritual). Or why not 2xp to turn into a flying T-Rex? Doesn't have to turn into a regular animal.<br /> <br /> Lunars may be able to turn into animals, but a sorcerer can give themselves the power to turn into anything, and Solars are better sorcerers than Lunars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T22:27:39-07:00","id":857506,"title":"","content":"Aquillion, how are you consistently so fantastic at this? Is the secret behind your success Glorious Solar Forum Prana, or is it the cinnamon swirls all over every bite?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T22:31:50-07:00","id":857510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/857445-i-am-worried-solars-won-t-be-the-best-at-shapeshifting-in-3e?p=857505#post857505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">JayTee, I'm afraid you're wrong, there's literally a merit for shooting fire.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that's just a merit that anyone can grab. Solars must have a native option to manipulate the elements, as anything else is objectively sub-optimal and damaging to the game line. Why haven't the devs fixed this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T22:33:57-07:00","id":857511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/857445-i-am-worried-solars-won-t-be-the-best-at-shapeshifting-in-3e?p=857510#post857510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that's just a merit that anyone can grab. Solars must have a native option to manipulate the elements, as anything else is objectively sub-optimal and damaging to the game line. Why haven't the devs fixed this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. I for one feel <i>incredibly </i>deprotagonised by the lack of native Solar bending charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T00:22:53-07:00","id":857550,"title":"","content":"It's blatantly obvious that Solars are <i>laughably underpowered</i> in relation to Lunar shapeshifting. This defies the Solar Eminence Doctrine!<br /> <br /> And we all know Solars can never escape Solars! Why hasn't this been errata'd yet?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T00:56:48-07:00","id":857565,"title":"","content":"Eh, don't worry. Shapeshifting is really just window dressing. We'll still have all the mechanical effects available in more powerful forms, they just won't <i>look </i>like shapeshifting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T01:02:16-07:00","id":857570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/857445-i-am-worried-solars-won-t-be-the-best-at-shapeshifting-in-3e?p=857511#post857511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed. I for one feel <i>incredibly </i>deprotagonised by the lack of native Solar bending charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it good or bad that the first time I read it I thought of charms that emulate Bender of Futurama fame before I thought The Last Airbender?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T01:03:30-07:00","id":857572,"title":"","content":"I know it's easy to miss, but the reason it looks like Solars don't have elemental manipulation is that they're not doing it the Dragon-blooded way with Dragon-Graced Prana Technique. They're going to master each element as completely as the Dragon-blooded master elements in general. Water will come from Sail, Wood will come from Survival, Earth will probably come from Craft, and I'm not sure about Air and Fire. Of course, those could all have changed between the backer PDF and release, though it's pretty unlikely.<br /> EDIT: And, of course, that leaves a full 20 Abilities for shapeshifting, destiny manipulation and necromancy. Man, it's a good thing they upped the wordcount, or there wouldn't have been any room for the iconic Solar charms!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T01:38:34-07:00","id":857580,"title":"","content":"Don't you guys know? Solars are already the best shapeshifters, all they have to do is lie so well to the world as a stunt that reality itself believes it and makes them shapeshifters to correct its mistake. <br /> <br /> But really, I'm more worried that Solars won't be able to switch their cybernetic charms around for maximum versatility, after all, we all know the versatile nature of humanity and how specialization is for insects! and lets not forget how we only get two different charms to take spirits powers for ourselves! When are we going to have them permanently and with the ability to enhance those charms to be better than the originals? or how can we forget that humans are better at being strange alien inhuman things than strange alien inhuman things, how is THAT expressed in the Solar charmset huh? these are important things that they need to spend the wordcount on!<br /> <br /> and while we're at it, where is the Shard where Solars are the only Exalts in existence and play all out all the same events in canon Exalted but better than all the other splats? We could have Solars choosing the vision of Bronze to manipulate the Solars to overthrow the Solars but better, then issue in the Solar Shogunate that goes into <i>better decline </i>than the Dragon-Blooded one, and has a better warring state period to! Then of course the Solars unleash the Solar Contagion on the Solars that is even better than the Great Contagion, which causes 90% of Creation to die but better. Then the Solar Empress defeats the Solar Contagion and the Solar Folk with the Realm Defense Grid/Sword of Creation, and begins to rule the Solar Empire, which is in a state of bronze age decadence and whatnot but better than the Scarlet Empire at doing so. Then the Solars return to overthrow the Solars and retake their rightful place in Creation with Solars as their servants. Cuts out all the unnecessary bits of having Exalts other than Solars exist, I say!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6018-raziere","name":"Raziere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6018_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T02:02:16-07:00","id":857586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/857445-i-am-worried-solars-won-t-be-the-best-at-shapeshifting-in-3e?p=857491#post857491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Common misconception: you actually don't need charms to introduce a fact. 3 dots is enough, and with that and a Solar excellency you can easily hit the required difficulty to introduce the fact that you're a shapeshifter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why bother introducing the fact that you're a shapeshifter? When someone tries to attack your bookish scholar in a dark alleyway or something, just say &quot;Little do you know that according to my years of study as a learned naturalist, I'm a bear.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 04-04-2016, 01:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T02:09:17-07:00","id":857587,"title":"","content":"What? The shapeshifting Charms are right there in the book. The trick is that you can only find them by looking in the index first and THEN going to the indicated page. It really is a magical layout they made for the new edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T04:55:19-07:00","id":857625,"title":"","content":"I was already to argue that Solars can't be the best at Astrology, but then I saw the light. The Sun is a Star! Not only is it a star, it's the largest of the stars in Creation! Of course Solars should be the best at Astrology! <br /> <br /> /Mind Blown","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T06:18:47-07:00","id":857658,"title":"","content":"{checks date} Fine. But no more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T10:43:34-07:00","id":857792,"title":"","content":"Building off of what Raziere said, but sometimes I feel it might be healthier for the game as a whole if we were to cut out the other splats and allow their special abilities to be optional avenues of power for Solars, similar to Sorcery or Martial arts. I feel it would really diversify the Solar's options and allow for more varied characters, as well as smooth over the setting's rather messy history and sociopolitical situation. That way you could have a cyborg Solar, a fate ninja Solar, a shapeshifter Solar, and an elemental Solar all in the same circle without worrying about having to justify it.<br /> <br /> This would be a natural evolution of the game line, and would work well for a wider verity of games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T11:53:34-07:00","id":857835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raziere</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/857445-i-am-worried-solars-won-t-be-the-best-at-shapeshifting-in-3e?p=857580#post857580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't you guys know? Solars are already the best shapeshifters, all they have to do is lie so well to the world as a stunt that reality itself believes it and makes them shapeshifters to correct its mistake.<br /> <br /> But really, I'm more worried that Solars won't be able to switch their cybernetic charms around for maximum versatility, after all, we all know the versatile nature of humanity and how specialization is for insects! and lets not forget how we only get two different charms to take spirits powers for ourselves! When are we going to have them permanently and with the ability to enhance those charms to be better than the originals? or how can we forget that humans are better at being strange alien inhuman things than strange alien inhuman things, how is THAT expressed in the Solar charmset huh? these are important things that they need to spend the wordcount on!<br /> <br /> and while we're at it, where is the Shard where Solars are the only Exalts in existence and play all out all the same events in canon Exalted but better than all the other splats? We could have Solars choosing the vision of Bronze to manipulate the Solars to overthrow the Solars but better, then issue in the Solar Shogunate that goes into <i>better decline </i>than the Dragon-Blooded one, and has a better warring state period to! Then of course the Solars unleash the Solar Contagion on the Solars that is even better than the Great Contagion, which causes 90% of Creation to die but better. Then the Solar Empress defeats the Solar Contagion and the Solar Folk with the Realm Defense Grid/Sword of Creation, and begins to rule the Solar Empire, which is in a state of bronze age decadence and whatnot but better than the Scarlet Empire at doing so. Then the Solars return to overthrow the Solars and retake their rightful place in Creation with Solars as their servants. Cuts out all the unnecessary bits of having Exalts other than Solars exist, I say!</div> </div> </div> </div>I can no longer tell who's being sincere or ironic in this thread, but a Shard where every Exalt is a Solar and it's a constant fuckfest of murder, intrigue, and revolt sounds a lot like Kill Six Billion Demons so I am surprisingly-okay with this premise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T12:46:58-07:00","id":857866,"title":"","content":"Bestest April Fool's is best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T13:31:43-07:00","id":857888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/857445-i-am-worried-solars-won-t-be-the-best-at-shapeshifting-in-3e?p=857835#post857835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can no longer tell who's being sincere or ironic in this thread, but a Shard where every Exalt is a Solar and it's a constant fuckfest of murder, intrigue, and revolt sounds a lot like Kill Six Billion Demons so I am surprisingly-okay with this premise.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are already all Solars. Its just they each have a unique caste assigned at the moment of Exaltation that includes proprietary charms much like those DB bloodline only charms the Devs talked about. So Shapeshifting Caste Solars can't use the charms from Ability Caste Solars can't use the Charms from Cyborg Caste Solars. They is a special expansion of Supernal Abilities that lets you customize your Solar even more. For some reason the backer preview used the words Exalt or Exalted in a lot of places it should have used Solar and forgot to include a full description of the Supernal Caste rules. No doubt it will be fixed in the release copy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T14:12:02-07:00","id":857912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/857445-i-am-worried-solars-won-t-be-the-best-at-shapeshifting-in-3e?p=857570#post857570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it good or bad that the first time I read it I thought of charms that emulate Bender of Futurama fame before I thought The Last Airbender?</div> </div> </div> </div>The answer is yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T02:31:05-07:00","id":858240,"title":"","content":"All mortals are also already secretly Solars. They were all Exalted by the Unconquered Sun for being paragons of... er.... mortalness, and just figured, why fix what ain't broken?<br /> <br /> You may have also heard a rumour that the Exigents involves both the fire of the Unconquered Sun and another god. Naturally, this is false and it is the Unconquered Sun alone, so of course, they are Solars. It's just that the Unconquered Sun is such a great guy he doesn't sweat allowing others to pretend to have a little participation in things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}